<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1169" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄδεια</span></b>  (A), ἡ,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδεής Ἀ</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>freedom from fear</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.20
			</span></i>; esp.<i>safe conduct, amnesty, indemnity</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδείην διδόναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.121
				</span></i>
			.
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζ́; τοῖς ἄλλοις ἄ. ἐδώκατε οἰκεῖν
					τὴν σφετέραν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antipho
					5.77
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ἀ. εἶναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.120
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ἀ. οὐ ποιεῖσθαι τὸ
			λέγειν</span> to hold it not <i>safe</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				9.42
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ σῶμά τινος εἰς ἄ. καθιστάναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					2.15
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν σωμάτων ἄ. ποιεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					3.58
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολλὴν ἄ. αὐτοῖς ἐψηφισμένοι ἔσεσθε
					ποιεῖν ὅτι ἂν βούλωνται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					22.19
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. τινι παρασκευάσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					16.13
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				13.17
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρέχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					21.210
				</span></i>
			; opp. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. εὑρίσκεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					And.
					1.34
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				24.47
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαμβάνειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					18.286
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδείας τυγχάνειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					5.6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ μὴ πάσχειν ἄδειαν ἤγετε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					19.149
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετὰ πάσης ἀδείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					18.305
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετ᾽ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					22.25
				</span></i>
			:—also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆς ἄ.</span> a
				<i>secure</i> dwelling-place, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				447
			</span></i>:—<i>licence</i> to bring forward proposals or
			make charges, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				24.45
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Per.</u>
				31
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Lit.
			Crit., <i>licence</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. ποιητική</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.D.
					<u>Pron.</u>
					38.3
				</span></i>
			, al., <i><span class="en">
				Him.
				<u>Or.</u>
				1.1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κωμική</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.D.
					<u>Pron.</u>
					69.19
				</span></i>
			.</div>
